+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"bug-002","node_id":"N2","attempt":4,"source":"reviewer","source_ref":"docs/trace/bug-002/N2/verdicts/A3-reviewer.json R1, R2 (verdict FAIL at 93eed277; R3 P2 carried to N4, out of scope)","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"WB-7","layer":"api","files":["src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/app/workbench/RequestsDrawer.tsx","src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/TwoDecimalPlacesConverter.cs","src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/app/data/api.ts","src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/kit/patterns/json-viewer/JsonViewer.tsx"],"root_cause":"Layer: the Docket workbench drawer adapter. The schema has no web layer, so 'api' marks the screen that calls the API, as in A1 and A2. Symptom (R1): the requests drawer shows money tokens the API never sent: 803.40 shows as 803.4, 500.00 as 500, and a 0.00 refund as 0. The orchestrator's node check shows the same. Cause: forDisplay at RequestsDrawer.tsx:13 indents a JSON body by sending it through JSON.parse and then JSON.stringify. That turns every JSON number into a JS double and writes it back in the shortest form, so the trailing zeros are lost. Both the request (:21) and the response (:22) go through it. The token is exact on the wire, because the API writes every decimal raw with at least two places (TwoDecimalPlacesConverter.cs:7-9, :16-17, :19-29). The log keeps it exact too, because loggingFetch stores response.clone().text() unchanged (api.ts:442-445). The kit drawer prints request.exchange as text unchanged (kit InspectorDrawer.tsx:181-188). So the only change happens at RequestsDrawer.tsx:13. The comment at :10, 'indented for reading', describes a whitespace-only change that the code doesn't make. Rule: WB-7, 'The exact request and response of every action' (docs/ui-requirements.md:174). A re-serialised body is not the exact response. The kit already sets the contract this breaks. JsonViewer re-indents 'never re-parsed into other numbers, so \"615.40\" stays \"615.40\"' (JsonViewer.tsx:7). It does this with a token-copying walk over the raw text (:23-67), and parses only to check the text is valid (:69-76). The /requests page uses it (RequestLogPage.tsx:75), so the drawer is the one place that goes the other way. That indent helper isn't exported from the kit barrel (kit/patterns/json-viewer/index.ts:1-2), and a build node may not change the kit. Not a recurrence: forDisplay came in with this node's A1 I13 indent work, and no earlier fingerprint names it. Direction: the drawer has to indent the received text by changing whitespace only, copying every token (numbers, strings, literals) character for character, and use JSON parsing only to decide whether a body is JSON. A body that isn't JSON stays exactly as received, as now. The wire text in the log stays untouched. Same cause as I2, from the test side: I2 explains why no test caught this one.","fingerprint":"WB-7|src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/app/workbench/RequestsDrawer.tsx|display-reserialises-json-drops-number-tokens","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given a stubbed claims POST whose raw response text is hand-written to hold \"amount\":803.40, \"amount\":500.00 and \"amount\":0.00 (compact, as the API writes it), When the page sends it through browserDeps().fetch and the RequestsDrawer shows that exchange, Then the exchange's pre text holds 803.40, 500.00 and 0.00 each as a whole token (not followed by another digit), holds no token 803.4 followed by a comma, brace or line end, and is still indented one key a line; and Given the same at 93eed277, Then it fails on the 803.40 assertion (unit/screens/wb-7-requests-drawer.test.tsx, WB-7 · title)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"WB-7","layer":"tests","files":["tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/screens/wb-7-requests-drawer.test.tsx","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/e2e/N2/wb-7.spec.ts","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/e2e/W1/support/workbench.ts","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/screens/support/app.tsx","docs/ui/fixture/api/050-get-1-amount-803-40-is-written-803-40-201.json"],"root_cause":"Symptom (R2): every WB-7 test passed at d5b1e69c with I1's defect in place. Note: the verdict cites wb-7-requests-drawer.test.tsx:651, but the file has 105 lines at HEAD. That line is probably in the packet diff, so the lines below are at HEAD. Cause, unit: the stub network builds the claims answer as JSON.stringify(claim.responseBody) (wb-7-requests-drawer.test.tsx:31). claim comes from recordedExchange (support/app.tsx:16-21), which JSON.parses a recording whose bodies are stored as parsed JSON. 050's item is titled 'amount 803.40 is written 803.40', yet it holds \"amount\": 803.4 (050-...json:59, :80, :88). So the stubbed wire text can never carry a trailing-zero token. The fetch is rebuilt the same way at :102. The assertions at :88-96 check only that the body isn't on one line and that each key starts an indented line, never a value token. Cause, e2e: watchApi JSON.parses every response (workbench.ts:375-380). leaves() turns each number back into text with String(value) (wb-7.spec.ts:26-31), and :59-60, :79-80 and :99 assert it with toContainText, a substring match. String(803.4) is a substring of both '803.4' and '803.40', so those tests pass whether or not I1 is fixed. The amounts used (611.29 at :68, 633.41 at :86) have no trailing zero, so even an exact match couldn't tell the difference. The Acceptance 4 test (:214-242) checks layout only. So the suite's expected values are derived through the same JS-number round trip that causes I1, which is a tests cause, separate from the code cause I1. Not a recurrence. Direction: add a red test whose expected text is the raw token as the API writes it, never a value rebuilt from parsed JSON. It needs a hand-written raw response body, because the recordings in docs/ui/fixture/api/ have lost the tokens. It must fail at 93eed277. If an e2e is added on the live API, read the expected token from the raw response text (response.text()), not from watchApi's parsed body, and sell an amount with a trailing zero. Weaken nothing.","fingerprint":"WB-7|tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/screens/wb-7-requests-drawer.test.tsx|expected-values-derived-from-parsed-json-no-token-check","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the unit stub network answering the claims POST with the hand-written raw text {\"reference\":\"N2U-TOK\",\"amount\":803.40,\"refund\":0.00} (status 201), When the drawer shows that exchange, Then its text contains 803.40 and 0.00 as whole tokens, and the test fails at 93eed277; optionally Given a policy sold on the live API with amount 803.40, When the sell inspector shows the 201, Then every number token in the raw response text (response.text()) appears verbatim in the shown exchange (unit/screens/wb-7-requests-drawer.test.tsx; e2e/N2/wb-7.spec.ts)","untestable_reason":null}],"previous_attempts":["attempt 1: green 40239581 passed N2's own tests; gate.e2e FAIL with W2/W3 functional breaks and new sell/cancel inspector screenshots (A1 I1-I7); the forDisplay indent came in during the A1 I13 work and no finding covered value tokens.","attempt 2: gate.e2e FAIL at 02d7dee9, regression only; the sell receipt h2 was covered by the sticky drawer (A2 I1, I2); inv-011 decided.","attempt 3: A2 fix 17418366; gates pass at d5b1e69c (e2e functional 809/809, regression within inv-011 #2); reviewer FAIL at 93eed277 on R1 (drawer re-serialises JSON numbers) and R2 (no test checks exact tokens); security PASS. These are new causes, not a recurrence of any A1 or A2 fingerprint."]}
